## B.3 Component architecture (Mermaid C4 Container level)

```mermaid
C4Container
  title Container diagram for OAuth feature

  Person(user, "B2B User", "Authenticated end user")

  Container_Boundary(spa, "Web SPA") {
    Container(nextjs, "Next.js 15", "TypeScript", "Renders UI, manages tokens via httpOnly cookies")
  }

  Container_Boundary(api, "Auth Service") {
    Container(fastapi, "FastAPI", "Python 3.12", "Handles OAuth flows, token validation")
    ContainerDb(postgres, "PostgreSQL 16", "Existing prod cluster", "Stores users, sessions, refresh tokens")
  }

  Container_Ext(keycloak, "Keycloak", "Existing realm 'b2b'", "OIDC provider")

  Rel(user, nextjs, "Uses", "HTTPS")
  Rel(nextjs, fastapi, "API calls", "HTTPS + httpOnly cookie")
  Rel(fastapi, keycloak, "OIDC flows", "HTTPS + mTLS")
  Rel(fastapi, postgres, "Reads/writes", "TCP")
```

**Trust boundaries:**
- Internet ↔ SPA: TLS 1.3, HSTS
- SPA ↔ Auth Service: httpOnly cookies, CSRF token
- Auth Service ↔ Keycloak: mTLS + client credentials
- Auth Service ↔ PostgreSQL: VPC internal, network policy

**Existing components touched (mandatory enumeration — anti-Böckeler):**
- Keycloak realm `b2b` — existing, no changes (out of scope)
- PostgreSQL `prod-eu-1` — new tables only (additive)
- Frontend session middleware in `apps/web/middleware.ts` — extended

## B.4 Tech stack constraints

```markdown
### MUST
- Frontend: Next.js 15.x
- Backend: FastAPI 0.115+ with Pydantic v2
- DB: PostgreSQL 16 (existing prod cluster `prod-eu-1`)
- Auth: OIDC via existing Keycloak realm `b2b` (NE custom JWT)
- Observability: OpenTelemetry + existing Grafana stack

### MAY
- Caching: Redis MAY (pokud justified v ADR), default no-cache
- Background jobs: existing Celery setup if needed

### MUST NOT
- ❌ MongoDB / non-relational primary store
- ❌ Custom auth implementation
- ❌ AWS Lambda (org runs k8s)
- ❌ Bleeding-edge libraries < 6 mo since stable release
```

